SDE WM: keybinds with onRelease="yes" act when the key is let go.

0.2.0 Alpha 4 (docs/SHORTCUTS.md in SDE). SDE's configuration has always
bound the Win key alone (Super_L, onRelease="yes") to the Start menu, but
Openbox does not know that attribute: the menu opened as soon as Win went
down, so every Win+key shortcut (Win+D, Win+E, Win+Left ...) also opened
the Start menu, which then took the keyboard. With the Windows shortcuts
of SDE 0.2.0 Alpha 4 that is no longer acceptable.

* A keybind with onRelease="yes" runs its actions when its key is let go,
  and only when no other key and no mouse button was pressed while it was
  down: Win alone opens the Start menu, Win+D only shows the desktop.
* Other keybinds are unchanged; the flag survives a keyboard mapping
  change (rebind).

